(5532353, 799824, 83313, '<td valign="top">Nice contrasty b/w work, and I like the detail you squeezed into this. The guy being cut off at the frame edge is the only real critique I have.</td>', 'Nice contrasty b/w work, and I like the detail you squeezed into this. The guy being cut off at the frame edge is the only real critique I have.', '2009-06-17 01:18:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5532365, 799767, 107145, '<td valign="top">`</td>', '`', '2009-06-17 01:21:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(5532366, 799854, 83313, '<td valign="top">The crop seems a little tight and awkward for my tastes. The image comes off to me slightly flat as well. Some minor adjustments could perk it up a bit. Sorry to have to be so harsh with what is probably your first vote.</td>', 'The crop seems a little tight and awkward for my tastes. The image comes off to me slightly flat as well. Some minor adjustments could perk it up a bit. Sorry to have to be so harsh with what is probably your first vote.', '2009-06-17 01:21:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5532378, 799513, 83313, '<td valign="top">Well, she IS constructing something! Cute kid and if anyone calls this DNMC, send them my way and I will beat them with my shoehorn.</td>', 'Well, she IS constructing something! Cute kid and if anyone calls this DNMC, send them my way and I will beat them with my shoehorn.', '2009-06-17 01:23:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(5532397, 799240, 83313, '<td valign="top">Seems a little soft on detail, so I looked at the file size. Congratulations! You get one of my (in)famous comments about JPEG compression!<br/> <br/>There is some excessive JPEG compression taking away a lot of detail. Your file size is only 82k and you could have used up to 150k for this challenge. Compression kills detail. Always use the least compression you can get away with and still come in under challenge limits. Most image editors have that ability to adjust compression somewhere in the file save dialog. <br/> <br/>Also, you should use the maximum image size allowed of 640 pixels on at least one side of your entry. Especially important for a highly detailed image like this.<br/> <br/>Hope this helped some.</td>', 'Seems a little soft on detail, so I looked at the file size. Congratulations! You get one of my (in)famous comments about JPEG compression! There is some excessive JPEG compression taking away a lot of detail. Your file size is only 82k and you could have used up to 150k for this challenge. Compression kills detail. Always use the least compression you can get away with and still come in under challenge limits. Most image editors have that ability to adjust compression somewhere in the file save dialog.  Also, you should use the maximum image size allowed of 640 pixels on at least one side of your entry. Especially important for a highly detailed image like this. Hope this helped some.', '2009-06-17 01:28:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5532398, 799085, 86447, '<td valign="top">"Take a picture of something in the process of being built."<br/> <br/>Dang.  I had this a 7, until I re-read the description.   5   *sigh*</td>', '"Take a picture of something in the process of being built." Dang.  I had this a 7, until I re-read the description.   5   *sigh*', '2009-06-17 01:28:42.000000', NULL, 1),
